 arrived backstage, she saw the act going on just before her: a local duo called the Edwards Sisters, so dazzling that she lost her nerve entirely. Facing a rowdy Apollo crowd dishevelled, wearing men's boots and ill-fitting clothes — she made a split-second decision to sing instead. She won the $25 first prize. The theatre, judging her appearance too untidy, refused to give her the other half of the prize: a week's paid engagement on the Apollo stage. Undeterred, she entered every talent contest she could find across the city and won them all. Within a year she was performing professionally; within a decade she was the most celebrated jazz vocalist in America. X recorded more than 200 albums over five decades and won 13 Grammy Awards, including the first Grammy ever awarded for Best Jazz Vocal Performance. Her technical range spanned three octaves. The composer Ira Gershwin said: “I never knew how good our songs were until I heard X sing them.” Her manager Norman Granz once had to threaten to cancel a tour unless a Dallas nightclub agreed to desegregate — they agreed. She was known as the First Lady of Song, the Queen of Jazz, and, simply, “The Lady.” ID X (10 points).", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-25T16:22:53Z", "username": "Abhishek Saluja", "text": "Ella", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-25T16:22:55Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "Ella", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-25T16:22:56Z", "username": "Abhishek Saluja", "text": "Fitzgerald", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-25T16:22:57Z", "username": "Chinmay Mehta", "text": "Al Ella", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-25T16:22:59Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "Fitzgerald", "role": 